* GITVOCDROP - the engine op, as a SUBROUTINE.  See BP/GITSTATUS.
*
* ONE ARGUMENT, AND IT IS THE LIST.  GIT.OBJ calls this as GITVOCDROP(list, out)
* -- the repository is not passed, so the C half supplies ".git" exactly as the
* MVX one does.  The type table is per MV system and lives in mv_voc_class();
* the verb must not carry its own copy (mv_git#133).
      SUBROUTINE GITVOCDROP(LIST, ANS)
      DEFC VAR JBGITVOCDROP(VAR, VAR)
      ANS = ""
      X = JBGITVOCDROP(LIST, ANS)
      RETURN
